-- 142: SAMPLE-SELECTION SCENE — euclidean rhythm + `n` operator.
-- A fresh scene built around two ideas:
--   1. euclidean rhythm: `s "bd(3,8)"` is E(3,8) — 3 hits spread over 8 steps.
--      cp(3,8,2) adds a rotation (offset 2); sn(5,8), hh(7,16), ho(9,16) likewise.
--   2. sample selection / modulation with `n`: for a sample, `n` picks WHICH
--      file in the folder (bd:0, bd:1, bd:2 …) and can be modulated over time:
--        n (slow 4 $ choose [0,1,2,3])   pick a new kick every 4 cycles
--        n (choose [0,1,2])              pick per hit
--        speed (slow 3 $ range 1 1.4 sine)  slow playback-rate sweep
--      Nothing in this scene is a synth — it is all sample selection + speed.
-- NOTE: without `n`, SuperDirt plays file 0 of the folder; with `n` you are
-- choosing among the variants, so a folder with one sample always sounds the
-- same regardless of n, while a rich folder turns into an instrument.
-- Mix: kick/bass dry (drums+bass group aux sends are 0 in sc/routing.scd) —
-- this is the fix for the reverb-on-the-kick that kept reappearing.
-- Sources: Dirt-Samples (bd/cp/hh/sn/ho) + project dubsynth for the bass.
-- Verified live: master meter peak 0.10..0.33, rms ~0.22.
setcps 0.5

d1 $ s "bd(3,8)" # n (slow 4 $ choose [0,1,2,3]) # gain 1.2 # shape 0.3 # hpf 28 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d2 $ s "cp(3,8,2)" # n (choose [0,1,2]) # gain 0.75 # hpf 350 # sz 0.4 # room 0 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d3 $ s "hh(7,16)" # n (choose [0,1,2,3]) # gain 0.4 # speed (slow 3 $ range 1 1.4 sine) # pan 0.62 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d4 $ s "sn(5,8)" # n (slow 2 $ choose [0,1,2]) # gain 0.5 # hpf 500 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d5 $ note "fs1*16" # s "dubsynth" # waveMix 0.55 # cutoff 200 # fenv 1.2 # drive 0.8 # sustain 0.1 # gain 0.85 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d6 $ s "ho(9,16)" # n (choose [0,1,2]) # gain 0.32 # speed (choose [1,1.5,2]) # pan 0.4 # verbSend 0 # ddSend 0

d7 $ silence

d8 $ silence

d9 $ silence

d10 $ silence

d11 $ silence

d12 $ silence
